      "text": "whatsoever thou mightest be profited, Matt. 15:5 (Mark 7:11). what is a man profited, if he shall gain the whole world, Matt. 16:26 (Mark 8:36; D&C 88:33). the flesh profiteth nothing, John 6:63. circumcision … profiteth, if thou keep the law, Rom. 2:25. what profit is there of circumcision, Rom. 3:1. this I speak for your own profit, 1 Cor. 7:35. not seeking mine own profit, but the profit of many, 1 Cor. 10:33. Spirit is given to every man to profit, 1 Cor. 12:7. profited in the Jews’ religion above many, Gal. 1:14. if ye be circumcised, Christ shall profit you nothing, Gal. 5:2. bodily exercise profiteth little, 1 Tim. 4:8. thy profiting may appear to all, 1 Tim. 4:15. they strive not about words to no profit, 2 Tim. 2:14. word preached did not profit them, Heb. 4:2. What doth it profit … though a man say he hath faith, and have not works, James 2:14.",
